OL,3,GNEWSAHow 'doomed to fail' energy firm
OL,4,Acost taxpayers #40m
OL,5,
OL,6,FA council-owned company was set up to
OL,7,Fhelp people receive ethically sourced
OL,8,Fand low cost energy - yet ended up
OL,9,Fcosting city taxpayers #40m.
OL,11,FIt has come to light the final cost to
OL,12,Fcouncil taxpayers of the collapse of
OL,13,FBristol Energy is #39.3m, following
OL,14,Ffive years of liquidators winding up
OL,15,Fthe company by collecting the money it
OL,16,Fwas owed and paying off debts.
OL,18,FIn 2021, council auditors Grant
OL,19,FThornton criticised the decision making
OL,20,Fwhich saw large sums of public money
OL,21,Fbeing lost, and questioned why the
OL,22,Fcouncil kept propping it up.
